# The sidecar Caddy (plan §4.8.3 "Where headers live", Q5): a plain reverse_proxy to the image, which owns every app
# header. No `header` directive (reverse_proxy adds upstream headers, so a set here would send a second copy) and no
# `encode` (it compresses identity responses, drops Accept-Ranges and rewrites ETags). `compression off`: otherwise
# the transport asks the image for gzip when the client sent no Accept-Encoding and decompresses it, so the client
# gets identity bytes under the .gz variant's ETag (#306, ORCH-NOTE 6086179079 on #110).
:8081 {
	reverse_proxy app:8080 {
		transport http {
			compression off
		}
	}
}
